<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Othello</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1603</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Othello is a tragedy by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-shakespeare">William Shakespeare</a>, written around 1603 and first published in 1622. It tells of a Moorish general in the service of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> who is driven by his scheming ensign Iago to murder his wife, Desdemona. Scholars have linked the play's Moorish hero to English interest in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>, including the visit of the Moroccan embassy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-wahid-ben-messaoud">Abd al-Wahid ben Messaoud</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> in 1600.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/othello.jpg" alt="Othello" width="320" height="405" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Théodore Chassériau · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Othello_et_Desd%C3%A9mone_%C3%A0_Venise_-_Th%C3%A9odore_Chass%C3%A9riau_-_Mus%C3%A9e_du_Louvre_Peintures_RF_3897.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
